{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017NFWZsDD227fSysicF4Tfx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Anchor R&D Surface v3 â€” \"Mission Control\" â€” Master Plan (frozen design)\n2\t\n3\t> Crucible Stage 1 output, approved 2026-06-11. Supersedes nothing in v2 (which\n4\t> shipped to master) â€” it BUILDS ON v2 (sessions.py, summarizer.py,\n5\t> rnd_terminal.py, deliverables.py, job_runner.py, vendor/xterm). v3 reshapes the\n6\t> UX (thin rows, in-place expandable accurate summaries), turns the terminal into\n7\t> a persistent, isolated, real (ConPTY) multi-session window manager, adds clean\n8\t> stage handoffs + concurrency isolation, and makes the Anchor deliverable\n9\t> runnable.\n10\t\n11\t## North Star (locked)\n12\t\n13\tTurn the Anchor dashboard into a **durable mission-control for trio-driven R&D**.\n14\tEvery project is a thin, full-width row with an accurate, auto-generated summary.\n15\tClicking any session expands a concise, **cached, in-place** summary (when Â·\n16\twhat-was-asked Â· North-Star Â· clickable doc links Â· effort in tokens+time) â€”\n17\tnever a separate \"no summary\" page. Trio work runs as **persistent, isolated,\n18\tserver-side terminal sessions** managed like stacking windows â€” open / attach /\n19\tminimize / kill-with-confirm, status-colored, surviving disconnect â€” where\n20\tlaunching a session **feels exactly like a real Claude/Gemini terminal**, hands\n21\toff cleanly stageâ†’stage, and never lets a planning session collide with a\n22\trunning build.\n23\t\n24\t## Locked decisions (Stage 0/1 user gates)\n25\t\n26\t1. **Terminal substrate = real ConPTY** (via `pywinpty`). This consciously WAIVES\n27\t   Anchor's \"stdlib-only / no native assets\" rule **for the terminal subsystem\n28\t   only**. Everything else stays stdlib. The subsystem degrades gracefully (and\n29\t   the dashboard still works) if `pywinpty` is absent.\n30\t2. **Summaries = proactive background generation, cached.** Generated once\n31\t   (at discovery/rescan and right after a run completes); clicking shows a ready,\n32\t   cached summary in-place. Lazy \"generatingâ€¦\" only as a fallback.\n33\t3. **Concurrency isolation = git worktrees per session.** Each plan/research/build\n34\t   session runs in its own worktree+branch; trees never collide.\n35\t4. **Scope = one comprehensive plan** (all of v3 in a single Foreman build).\n36\t5. **ConPTY-under-service is gated by a Wave-1 spike that HALTS to the user if it\n37\t   fails** â€” no silent downgrade.\n38\t6. **Status colors:** green = actively working (ignore) Â· amber = needs you / done\n39\t   (come look) Â· red = failed Â· grey = idle.\n40\t\n41\t## Real intent (Parable of the Oranges)\n42\t\n43\tAnchor is John's single pane of glass for managing every project across every\n44\ttrio stage, replacing the cognitive load of juggling many VS Code windows +\n45\tterminals. The deeper needs it must serve: (a) at-a-glance TRUTH of what exists /\n46\twhat's running / what needs attention; (b) frictionless DRIVE â€” start, attach,\n47\tminimize, kill durable server-side sessions like a window manager; (c) clean\n48\tCONCURRENCY â€” plan the next wave while a build runs, isolated; (d) faithful\n49\tHANDOFFS stageâ†’stage; (e) RUNNABLE deliverables. Bloat that doesn't serve this is\n50\tcut or Grasscatched.\n51\t\n52\t## Current-state ground truth (verified 2026-06-11)\n53\t\n54\t- The `anchor` NSSM service runs as **`.\\john`** with working Claude **subscription**\n55\t  creds (`C:\\Users\\john\\.claude\\.credentials.json`) + `claude.exe`/`gemini`/`node`\n56\t  on the service PATH. Live trio off the subscription from the server is viable\n57\t  (v2 terminals already spawn `claude`). So \"no summary\" is a UX/architecture\n58\t  issue, NOT creds.\n59\t- v2 summaries are generated **lazily on click into a separate `/summary` page**\n60\t  that renders an empty/failed state when generation hasn't run or yields no\n61\t  grounded claims â€” this is exactly the \"hit summary â†’ no summary\" symptom.\n62\t- v2 terminal = a structured **stream-json REPL** that auto-seeds the lane skill\n63\t  (hence the \"unintelligible researchPrime internals\" dump) and whose interactive\n64\t  gate-answer path is empirically fragile (AskUserQuestion can't be answered\n65\t  cleanly). It is NOT a faithful terminal.\n66\t- v2 tiles are small squares wasting the right half of each row.\n67\t- Anchor's own deliverable (the `anchor_gui.py` server) is not represented.\n68\t\n69\t## Architecture (frozen)\n70\t\n71\t### A. Thin full-width project rows\n72\tReplace the square `rnd-tile` (in `anchor_gui.render_projects_view_html`) with a\n73\tone-line, full-width row: name Â· accurate summary Â· per-lane mini-counts Â· a\n74\tstatus dot. Click â†’ opens the project window. Lifecycle controls (P1/P2, archive,\n75\tnotes, rescan) move into a hover/kebab menu so the row stays thin.\n76\t\n77\t### B. Accurate, proactive, cached summaries (project + session)\n78\tEvolve `summarizer.py` so a background job generates each summary ONCE (on\n79\tdiscovery/rescan and right after a run completes) and caches it. Content fixed to\n80\tbe real and concise: **when-run (date) Â· what-was-asked (the seed/intent) Â·\n81\tNorth-Star (extracted from the session's MASTER-PLAN) Â· documents produced\n82\t(master plan / implementation plan / report â€¦) as clickable links that open\n83\tnicely-rendered markdown in a new tab Â· effort = tokens + wall-clock** from the\n84\t`job_runner` cost records. Imported sessions honestly show \"imported â€” no run\n85\tmetrics.\" The PROJECT summary is generated the same way from CLAUDE.md + recent\n86\tplan docs + deliverables (replaces the weak first-paragraph blurb).\n87\t\n88\t### C. In-place expandable session summaries (kills the \"no summary\" page)\n89\tClicking a session tile in any lane EXPANDS an accordion **inline** in the Kanban\n90\tshowing the cached summary + doc links + a \"Launch new session\" button; collapse\n91\tto minimize. No navigation to `/summary`. The only new-tab is the rendered\n92\tmarkdown document itself (reuse `report_viewer`).\n93\t\n94\t### D. Persistent server-side session manager + real ConPTY terminals\n95\tA durable **session registry** (persisted under `.anchor/`, survives restart) +\n96\ta **ConPTY terminal manager** (`pty_manager.py`, pywinpty backend with a stub\n97\tbackend seam for tests via an env override). Each session is a genuine PTY\n98\trunning interactive `claude`/`gemini` (real TUI, user-driven; NO auto-seeded\n99\tskill, NO gate-answer hack). Processes run under the `anchor` service (as john)\n100\tand SURVIVE client disconnect; reattach replays the live screen buffer.\n101\t**Transport:** a minimal **stdlib hand-rolled WebSocket** endpoint carrying PTY\n102\tbytes both directions into the vendored **xterm.js**; **SSE-out + POST-in is the\n103\tfallback** if the WS proves troublesome. Terminal endpoints are **token-authed**\n104\t(they are an RCE surface; must not sit on the unauthenticated GET surface).\n105\t\n106\t### E. Stacking window-manager UI\n107\tA top bar of terse **status-colored buttons** (\"plan 1\", \"research 2\",\n108\t\"foreman 1\"); click to open/attach. Terminal windows **stack like bricks (2â€“3)**,\n109\tare draggable / resizable / minimizable; minimize keeps the process running; an\n110\t**X kills with an \"Are you sure?\" confirm**. Status colors per the locked mapping\n111\t(green/amber/red/grey). Reopening Anchor repopulates the running sessions and\n112\ttheir windows from the registry.\n113\t\n114\t### F. Git-worktree concurrency isolation\n115\tEach session runs in its own **git worktree + branch** under a managed,\n116\tgit-ignored location (outside the tracked tree), so a planning session can't\n117\tdirty a running Foreman build's tree. Worktree created on launch; removed on kill\n118\t(with confirm). Results are merged back deliberately (a session can be\n119\tmerged/inspected when done). A reaper cleans orphaned worktrees.\n120\t\n121\t### G. Stage handoffs\n122\tLaunching a build/execution session finds the **most-recent plan set** (from the\n123\t`.anchor` store / sessions) and asks \"execute on this plan set?\", pre-staging its\n124\tworktree and printing the plan paths in the terminal for the user to confirm/run.\n125\tGeneral principle: each lane's \"Launch new session\" can seed context from the\n126\tprior stage's outputs, all discoverable from the dashboard + the Anchor.md/.anchor\n127\treference.\n128\t\n129\t### H. Runnable Anchor deliverable\n130\tPin `anchor_gui.py` as the Anchor project's deliverable. Its **Run** action spins\n131\tup a **preview instance on an OS-assigned ephemeral port** (in a worktree/copy,\n132\tnever touching the live :8777 service or its single-instance guard) and opens the\n133\tbrowser to it; the preview is bounded and reaped.\n134\t\n135\t### I. Robustness / persistence\n136\tAll sessions, PTYs, worktrees, and preview servers run under the `anchor` service\n137\ton gwl-server â†’ they survive RDP disconnect / client crash. The session registry\n138\tis persisted; on reconnect the dashboard reflects true live state. A reaper\n139\thandles dead/hung sessions, orphan worktrees, and stale preview servers.\n140\t\n141\t## Constraints (binding)\n142\t\n143\t- **Stdlib-only EXCEPT the terminal subsystem**, which may use `pywinpty`\n144\t  (ConPTY). The native dep is isolated; if absent, the terminal subsystem\n145\t  degrades and the rest of the dashboard is unaffected. The distribution scan +\n146\t  healthcheck are updated to know about this single, declared exception.\n147\t- **No live `claude`/`gemini` in the test gate.** Model/PTY interactions are\n148\t  exercised via `tests/fake_claude.py` through `ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD` and a **stub\n149\t  PTY backend** (a fake pty-able child) â€” never live. The ConPTY-under-service\n150\t  empirical proof (Wave 1) is a documented manual/orchestrator check, separate\n151\t  from the pytest gate.\n152\t- **`anchor_gui.py` HTML is f-string-generated** (double literal braces);\n153\t  `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` is a RAW single-brace string.\n154\t- **Security:** terminal + preview-run + worktree endpoints are token-authed;\n155\t  GET endpoints stay read-only/unauthenticated; a real interactive terminal\n156\t  reachable over Tailscale is an RCE surface and must be behind the token.\n157\t- **Mirror** new backend data functions into `anchor.py` where natural.\n158\t- Runtime unchanged otherwise: NSSM service `anchor`, binds localhost:8777,\n159\t  single-instance guard on 8777.\n160\t\n161\t## Out of scope (Grass Catchers for later)\n162\t\n163\t- A general multi-user / multi-tenant terminal server.\n164\t- Cross-machine sync of `.anchor` / worktrees.\n165\t- Auto-merging session worktree results without user review.\n166\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25cad026-5d8a-48bd-9d51-30c755189e7a","uuid":"53bf825b-296e-483f-a034-f0214f4bcd66","timestamp":"2026-06-13T18:03:29.074Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Anchor\\planning\\rnd-v3\\MASTER-PLAN.md","content":"# Anchor R&D Surface v3 â€” \"Mission Control\" â€” Master Plan (frozen design)\n\n> Crucible Stage 1 output, approved 2026-06-11. Supersedes nothing in v2 (which\n> shipped to master) â€” it BUILDS ON v2 (sessions.py, summarizer.py,\n> rnd_terminal.py, deliverables.py, job_runner.py, vendor/xterm). v3 reshapes the\n> UX (thin rows, in-place expandable accurate summaries), turns the terminal into\n> a persistent, isolated, real (ConPTY) multi-session window manager, adds clean\n> stage handoffs + concurrency isolation, and makes the Anchor deliverable\n> runnable.\n\n## North Star (locked)\n\nTurn the Anchor dashboard into a **durable mission-control for trio-driven R&D**.\nEvery project is a thin, full-width row with an accurate, auto-generated summary.\nClicking any session expands a concise, **cached, in-place** summary (when Â·\nwhat-was-asked Â· North-Star Â· clickable doc links Â· effort in tokens+time) â€”\nnever a separate \"no summary\" page. Trio work runs as **persistent, isolated,\nserver-side terminal sessions** managed like stacking windows â€” open / attach /\nminimize / kill-with-confirm, status-colored, surviving disconnect â€” where\nlaunching a session **feels exactly like a real Claude/Gemini terminal**, hands\noff cleanly stageâ†’stage, and never lets a planning session collide with a\nrunning build.\n\n## Locked decisions (Stage 0/1 user gates)\n\n1. **Terminal substrate = real ConPTY** (via `pywinpty`). This consciously WAIVES\n   Anchor's \"stdlib-only / no native assets\" rule **for the terminal subsystem\n   only**. Everything else stays stdlib. The subsystem degrades gracefully (and\n   the dashboard still works) if `pywinpty` is absent.\n2. **Summaries = proactive background generation, cached.** Generated once\n   (at discovery/rescan and right after a run completes); clicking shows a ready,\n   cached summary in-place. Lazy \"generatingâ€¦\" only as a fallback.\n3. **Concurrency isolation = git worktrees per session.** Each plan/research/build\n   session runs in its own worktree+branch; trees never collide.\n4. **Scope = one comprehensive plan** (all of v3 in a single Foreman build).\n5. **ConPTY-under-service is gated by a Wave-1 spike that HALTS to the user if it\n   fails** â€” no silent downgrade.\n6. **Status colors:** green = actively working (ignore) Â· amber = needs you / done\n   (come look) Â· red = failed Â· grey = idle.\n\n## Real intent (Parable of the Oranges)\n\nAnchor is John's single pane of glass for managing every project across every\ntrio stage, replacing the cognitive load of juggling many VS Code windows +\nterminals. The deeper needs it must serve: (a) at-a-glance TRUTH of what exists /\nwhat's running / what needs attention; (b) frictionless DRIVE â€” start, attach,\nminimize, kill durable server-side sessions like a window manager; (c) clean\nCONCURRENCY â€” plan the next wave while a build runs, isolated; (d) faithful\nHANDOFFS stageâ†’stage; (e) RUNNABLE deliverables. Bloat that doesn't serve this is\ncut or Grasscatched.\n\n## Current-state ground truth (verified 2026-06-11)\n\n- The `anchor` NSSM service runs as **`.\\john`** with working Claude **subscription**\n  creds (`C:\\Users\\john\\.claude\\.credentials.json`) + `claude.exe`/`gemini`/`node`\n  on the service PATH. Live trio off the subscription from the server is viable\n  (v2 terminals already spawn `claude`). So \"no summary\" is a UX/architecture\n  issue, NOT creds.\n- v2 summaries are generated **lazily on click into a separate `/summary` page**\n  that renders an empty/failed state when generation hasn't run or yields no\n  grounded claims â€” this is exactly the \"hit summary â†’ no summary\" symptom.\n- v2 terminal = a structured **stream-json REPL** that auto-seeds the lane skill\n  (hence the \"unintelligible researchPrime internals\" dump) and whose interactive\n  gate-answer path is empirically fragile (AskUserQuestion can't be answered\n  cleanly). It is NOT a faithful terminal.\n- v2 tiles are small squares wasting the right half of each row.\n- Anchor's own deliverable (the `anchor_gui.py` server) is not represented.\n\n## Architecture (frozen)\n\n### A. Thin full-width project rows\nReplace the square `rnd-tile` (in `anchor_gui.render_projects_view_html`) with a\none-line, full-width row: name Â· accurate summary Â· per-lane mini-counts Â· a\nstatus dot. Click â†’ opens the project window. Lifecycle controls (P1/P2, archive,\nnotes, rescan) move into a hover/kebab menu so the row stays thin.\n\n### B. Accurate, proactive, cached summaries (project + session)\nEvolve `summarizer.py` so a background job generates each summary ONCE (on\ndiscovery/rescan and right after a run completes) and caches it. Content fixed to\nbe real and concise: **when-run (date) Â· what-was-asked (the seed/intent) Â·\nNorth-Star (extracted from the session's MASTER-PLAN) Â· documents produced\n(master plan / implementation plan / report â€¦) as clickable links that open\nnicely-rendered markdown in a new tab Â· effort = tokens + wall-clock** from the\n`job_runner` cost records. Imported sessions honestly show \"imported â€” no run\nmetrics.\" The PROJECT summary is generated the same way from CLAUDE.md + recent\nplan docs + deliverables (replaces the weak first-paragraph blurb).\n\n### C. In-place expandable session summaries (kills the \"no summary\" page)\nClicking a session tile in any lane EXPANDS an accordion **inline** in the Kanban\nshowing the cached summary + doc links + a \"Launch new session\" button; collapse\nto minimize. No navigation to `/summary`. The only new-tab is the rendered\nmarkdown document itself (reuse `report_viewer`).\n\n### D. Persistent server-side session manager + real ConPTY terminals\nA durable **session registry** (persisted under `.anchor/`, survives restart) +\na **ConPTY terminal manager** (`pty_manager.py`, pywinpty backend with a stub\nbackend seam for tests via an env override). Each session is a genuine PTY\nrunning interactive `claude`/`gemini` (real TUI, user-driven; NO auto-seeded\nskill, NO gate-answer hack). Processes run under the `anchor` service (as john)\nand SURVIVE client disconnect; reattach replays the live screen buffer.\n**Transport:** a minimal **stdlib hand-rolled WebSocket** endpoint carrying PTY\nbytes both directions into the vendored **xterm.js**; **SSE-out + POST-in is the\nfallback** if the WS proves troublesome. Terminal endpoints are **token-authed**\n(they are an RCE surface; must not sit on the unauthenticated GET surface).\n\n### E. Stacking window-manager UI\nA top bar of terse **status-colored buttons** (\"plan 1\", \"research 2\",\n\"foreman 1\"); click to open/attach. Terminal windows **stack like bricks (2â€“3)**,\nare draggable / resizable / minimizable; minimize keeps the process running; an\n**X kills with an \"Are you sure?\" confirm**. Status colors per the locked mapping\n(green/amber/red/grey). Reopening Anchor repopulates the running sessions and\ntheir windows from the registry.\n\n### F. Git-worktree concurrency isolation\nEach session runs in its own **git worktree + branch** under a managed,\ngit-ignored location (outside the tracked tree), so a planning session can't\ndirty a running Foreman build's tree. Worktree created on launch; removed on kill\n(with confirm). Results are merged back deliberately (a session can be\nmerged/inspected when done). A reaper cleans orphaned worktrees.\n\n### G. Stage handoffs\nLaunching a build/execution session finds the **most-recent plan set** (from the\n`.anchor` store / sessions) and asks \"execute on this plan set?\", pre-staging its\nworktree and printing the plan paths in the terminal for the user to confirm/run.\nGeneral principle: each lane's \"Launch new session\" can seed context from the\nprior stage's outputs, all discoverable from the dashboard + the Anchor.md/.anchor\nreference.\n\n### H. Runnable Anchor deliverable\nPin `anchor_gui.py` as the Anchor project's deliverable. Its **Run** action spins\nup a **preview instance on an OS-assigned ephemeral port** (in a worktree/copy,\nnever touching the live :8777 service or its single-instance guard) and opens the\nbrowser to it; the preview is bounded and reaped.\n\n### I. Robustness / persistence\nAll sessions, PTYs, worktrees, and preview servers run under the `anchor` service\non gwl-server â†’ they survive RDP disconnect / client crash. The session registry\nis persisted; on reconnect the dashboard reflects true live state. A reaper\nhandles dead/hung sessions, orphan worktrees, and stale preview servers.\n\n## Constraints (binding)\n\n- **Stdlib-only EXCEPT the terminal subsystem**, which may use `pywinpty`\n  (ConPTY). The native dep is isolated; if absent, the terminal subsystem\n  degrades and the rest of the dashboard is unaffected. The distribution scan +\n  healthcheck are updated to know about this single, declared exception.\n- **No live `claude`/`gemini` in the test gate.** Model/PTY interactions are\n  exercised via `tests/fake_claude.py` through `ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD` and a **stub\n  PTY backend** (a fake pty-able child) â€” never live. The ConPTY-under-service\n  empirical proof (Wave 1) is a documented manual/orchestrator check, separate\n  from the pytest gate.\n- **`anchor_gui.py` HTML is f-string-generated** (double literal braces);\n  `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` is a RAW single-brace string.\n- **Security:** terminal + preview-run + worktree endpoints are token-authed;\n  GET endpoints stay read-only/unauthenticated; a real interactive terminal\n  reachable over Tailscale is an RCE surface and must be behind the token.\n- **Mirror** new backend data functions into `anchor.py` where natural.\n- Runtime unchanged otherwise: NSSM service `anchor`, binds localhost:8777,\n  single-instance guard on 8777.\n\n## Out of scope (Grass Catchers for later)\n\n- A general multi-user / multi-tenant terminal server.\n- Cross-machine sync of `.anchor` / worktrees.\n- Auto-merging session worktree results without user review.\n","numLines":166,"startLine":1,"totalLines":166}}}
