{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01EKLsbSuDjGzAYcHmesqmJJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough grounding from all three member documents. Here is the summary.\n\n## Anchor R&D Surface v3 â€” \"Mission Control\" â€” Master Plan (frozen design)\n\n**What this session produced:** the frozen Crucible Stage 1 design (Master Plan), the Foreman-ready Stage 2 Implementation Plan, and the Execution Log for the v3 \"Mission Control\" overhaul.\n\n### North Star (locked)\n- Turn the Anchor dashboard into a **durable mission-control for trio-driven R&D**: every project is a thin, full-width row carrying an accurate auto-generated summary.\n- Clicking any session **expands a cached summary in-place** (when Â· what-was-asked Â· North-Star Â· clickable doc links Â· effort in tokens+time) â€” explicitly killing the v2 \"hit summary â†’ no summary\" separate-page symptom.\n- Trio work runs as **persistent, isolated, server-side terminal sessions** managed like stacking windows (open/attach/minimize/kill-with-confirm), status-colored, surviving client disconnect, and \"feels exactly like a real Claude/Gemini terminal.\"\n\n### Locked decisions (Stage 0/1 user gates)\n- **Terminal substrate = real ConPTY via `pywinpty`** â€” a conscious waiver of Anchor's stdlib-only / no-native-assets rule *for the terminal subsystem only*; everything else stays stdlib, and the subsystem degrades gracefully (dashboard still works) if `pywinpty` is absent.\n- **Summaries = proactive background generation, cached** â€” generated once at discovery/rescan and right after a run completes; lazy \"generatingâ€¦\" only as a fallback.\n- **Concurrency isolation = git worktrees per session** â€” each plan/research/build session runs in its own worktree+branch so trees never collide.\n- **Scope = one comprehensive plan** (all of v3 in a single Foreman build).\n- **ConPTY-under-service is gated by a Wave-1 spike that HALTS to the user if it fails** â€” no silent downgrade.\n- **Status colors:** green = actively working (ignore) Â· amber = needs you / done Â· red = failed Â· grey = idle.\n\n### Architecture (frozen) â€” nine pieces\n- **(A)** Thin full-width project rows replacing the square `rnd-tile`; lifecycle controls move to a hover/kebab menu.\n- **(B)** Accurate, proactive, cached project + session summaries from `job_runner` cost records; imported sessions honestly show \"imported â€” no run metrics.\"\n- **(C)** In-place expandable session accordions (no `/summary` navigation; the only new tab is rendered markdown via `report_viewer`).\n- **(D)** Durable session registry (persisted under `.anchor/`) + a ConPTY manager (`pty_manager.py`, pywinpty backend with a stub seam); sessions survive disconnect; transport is a **stdlib hand-rolled WebSocket** into vendored xterm.js, with SSE-out + POST-in as fallback; terminal endpoints are **token-authed** (RCE surface).\n- **(E)** Stacking window-manager UI â€” status-colored buttons, draggable/resizable/minimizable windows; X kills behind an \"Are you sure?\" confirm; reopening Anchor repopulates from the registry.\n- **(F)** Git-worktree concurrency isolation under a git-ignored managed base, with a reaper for orphans.\n- **(G)** Stage handoffs â€” a build launch finds the most-recent plan set and pre-stages its worktree.\n- **(H)** Runnable Anchor deliverable â€” `anchor_gui.py` pinned, **Run** spins up a preview on an OS-assigned ephemeral port (never the live :8777).\n- **(I)** Robustness/persistence under the `anchor` service on gwl-server, surviving RDP disconnect.\n\n### Binding constraints\n- Stdlib-only **except** the isolated `pywinpty` terminal subsystem; distro scan + healthcheck updated to know this single declared exception.\n- **No live `claude`/`gemini`/real-PTY in the pytest gate** â€” model calls via `tests/fake_claude.py` (`ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD`), PTY via a `stub` backend (`ANCHOR_PTY_BACKEND=stub`); the empirical ConPTY-under-service proof is a separate documented orchestrator check.\n- `anchor_gui.py` HTML is f-string-generated (doubled braces); `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` stays a RAW single-brace string. Mirror new data functions into `anchor.py`. Runtime unchanged (NSSM `anchor`, localhost:8777, single-instance guard).\n\n### Out of scope (Grass Catchers)\n- General multi-user/multi-tenant terminal server; cross-machine sync of `.anchor`/worktrees; auto-merging worktree results without user review.\n\n### Execution outcome (from the Execution Log)\n- Approved 2026-06-11. **Wave 1 ConPTY-under-service HARD GATE passed** â€” pytest 409 passed / 1 skipped, and the empirical spike proved a real pywinpty child echoing bytes under a simulated service context; **HALT condition not triggered**.\n- Subsequent waves stayed GREEN with growing test counts (Wave 2: 429, Wave 3: 449, Wave 4: 455 passed). Per the project memory, the full build landed all 10 waves GREEN (529 passed) and **merged to master 2026-06-12** (commit `208bce1`).\n\nAll claims above are grounded in the three member documents (MASTER-PLAN.md, IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md, EXECUTION-LOG.md); the final merge fact is corroborated by the v3 project memory."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1517,"cache_read_input_tokens":56418,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1517},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25cad026-5d8a-48bd-9d51-30c755189e7a","uuid":"785a8653-6b32-4d73-9ab1-9ef35c2c94b3","request_id":"req_011Cc1hYBmsnPNfZE8Qt2k7R"}
